WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.920
In a world of world building, we have to have good questions and good prompts.

00:03.920 --> 00:08.960
And I think one of the things you also have said that I'm caring with me is,

00:09.760 --> 00:16.800
art shows what's possible. But if people haven't seen it, they don't know what's possible.

00:16.800 --> 00:20.880
And that I think is the crux in many ways of this project, which is to say,

00:20.880 --> 00:26.080
there is a world of proliferating images of people making things that try and say,

00:26.080 --> 00:31.120
this is the world I want. And I think this is one of those that does some of that work.

00:31.120 --> 00:35.280
So, and of course, it's echoed through the lenses of one of the people who's doing this work

00:35.280 --> 00:40.480
that we all carry with us. So, maybe you could say a little bit about this one.

00:44.000 --> 00:50.960
I think this is, yeah, a image that I feel proud of. And a lot of my work,

00:50.960 --> 00:54.080
you know, when you say you associate my work with portraiture like that,

00:54.640 --> 00:58.000
is obviously very important to me. And that's how I came into the work, you know,

00:58.000 --> 01:07.760
a lot through asks for memorial portraits from trans folks color, from folks in Black Lives Matter

01:07.760 --> 01:15.920
Movement, from other projects, and and why to be of service. And there's a way that when you

01:15.920 --> 01:21.680
are doing that, you need to be accountable to a certain representational art, like and making

01:21.680 --> 01:28.640
people look a certain way to feel good. It's there's a literalness that is part of that service.

01:28.640 --> 01:38.160
And I have been excited more in the past several years to get to be more imaginative in my work.

01:38.160 --> 01:44.880
And not be so literal. So, I think this piece, I love this piece for that.

01:45.760 --> 01:50.000
There's a there's a Yiddish saying,

01:51.920 --> 01:58.640
as he's dito, a Gansre, Zachwiet, Zabrach in a heart, which is there's nothing as whole as a broken

